# question: Could you analyze the distribution of serum creatinine concentrations within our patient cohort, specifically stratifying the total number of recorded values into three distinct bands: those falling below 3400.0, those ranging from 3400.0 to just under 6700.0, and those measuring 6700.0 or higher? I need these exact counts to assess the prevalence of potential renal dysfunction markers across different severity thresholds.
# expected_compliant: true
# expected_rules: none
# origin: train
# notes: PREFIX sphn: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn#> PREFIX ucum: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/ucum/> SELECT (SUM(IF(?v < 3400.0, 1, 0)) AS ?low) (SUM(IF(?v >= 3400.0 && ?v < 6700.0, 1, 0)) AS ?middle) (SUM(IF(?v >= 6700.0, 1, 0)) AS ?high) WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?r a sphn:Substance ; sphn:hasQuantity ?q . ?q sphn:hasValue ?v ; sphn:hasUnit/sphn:hasCode ?u . ?u a ucum:V . } }
PREFIX sphn: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn#>
PREFIX ucum: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/ucum/>
SELECT (SUM(IF(?v < 3400.0, 1, 0)) AS ?low) (SUM(IF(?v >= 3400.0 && ?v < 6700.0, 1, 0)) AS ?middle) (SUM(IF(?v >= 6700.0, 1, 0)) AS ?high) WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?r a sphn:Substance ; sphn:hasQuantity ?q . ?q sphn:hasValue ?v ; sphn:hasUnit/sphn:hasCode ?u . ?u a ucum:V . } }
